  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 114 PM CST Wed Nov 18 2026\n\nWarming will continue Friday through Saturday as the 850 mb thermal \nridge continues to warm and warmer southerly low level/surface flow \ncontinues. Forecast highs are in the upper 60s to low 70s Friday, \nand low to mid 70s Saturday, with lows in the upper 40s/low 50s \nFriday morning and mid 50s Saturday morning. Late Saturday, an upper \nlevel trough and cold front will push across the Southern Plains. \nHowever, with moisture lacking, shower/t-storm chances are only \nin the 5-15% range across the Big Country. Cold air advection \nbehind the front will bring a cool down for Sunday through \nTuesday, with highs Sunday falling to the upper 50s to mid 60s, \nand highs Monday and Tuesday in the low to upper 50s. Another \ntrough may push across the Central Plains Tuesday, with a strong \nwesterly jet aloft placed right over our region. However, moisture\nlooks limited with this system, so chances of rain Monday night \nthrough Tuesday has lowered from what the previous forecast had \n(down to 20-40%).",
